A sample cross-option check can distinguish an option with repeated values from
one with a single value; it runs once per key rather than duplicating findings.
-- input/etc/fstab --
UUID=example /efi vfat x-systemd.idle-timeout=30s,umask=0077,x-systemd.idle-timeout=2min,x-systemd.requires=first.mount,x-systemd.requires=first.mount 0 2
-- expected/options.txt --
x-systemd.idle-timeout has-value=true value="30s"
umask has-value=true value="0077"
x-systemd.idle-timeout has-value=true value="2min"
x-systemd.requires has-value=true value="first.mount"
x-systemd.requires has-value=true value="first.mount"
-- expected/findings.txt --
info: example singleton x-systemd.idle-timeout has 2 occurrences
